{title: 527 - From Every Stormy Wind}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #527 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 527}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]From every stormy [Eb]wind that [Bb]blows,
[F7]From every swelling [Bb]tide of [F]woes,
There [Bb]is a calm, a sure re[F]treat:
[Bb]‘Tis found beneath the [Eb]mer[F7]cy [Bb]seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]There is a place [Eb]where Jesus sheds The oil [Bb]of gladness on our heads,
[F7]A place than all [Bb]besides more sweet; It [F]is the blood-bought mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]There is a scene [Eb]where spirits blend, Where [Bb]friend holds fellowship with friend;
[F7]Though sundered far, by [Bb]faith they meet Around [F]one common mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]There, there, on angel's [Eb]wings we soar, And [Bb]earthly cares molest no more,
[F7]And heaven comes down [Bb]our souls to greet, And [F]glory crowns the mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Bb]Ah! whither should [Eb]we flee for aid, [Bb]When tempted, desolate dismayed?
[F7]Or how the hosts [Bb]of sin defeat, Had [F]suffering saints no mercy seat?
{end_of_verse}
